 "verified-authority/distinct-root-names/equal-normalized-rule-body"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 before the canonical root-denotation identity"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "The semantic denotation cache key retained the queried root permission name. Two permission roots with identical normalized incoming rule bodies therefore occupied different entries even though their least-fixed-point grants were equal. The cache remained correct, but it could not reuse a shared subgraph across distinct top-level queries and was slower than completed-answer-only caching."
 :fix
 "Key a root denotation by its canonical indexed rule body while retaining the exact resource type, relation entity ids, target relation or permission nodes, target types, and recursively sorted subpaths. Prove that equal semantic rule bodies preserve equal root grants throughout fixed-point iteration, bridge exact indexed bodies to those semantic bodies under the compiler certificate, and regression-test both the intended equal-body reuse and non-collision for changed relations or target nodes."
 :closing-evidence
 ["formal/dafny/RootDenotation.dfy/EquivalentRuleBodiesHaveEqualSemanticDenotations"
